 
          <p>The calendar claims it&rsquo;s October already but the temperatures are still in denial. I can&rsquo;t remember ever experiencing the start of this month that warm. It&rsquo;s getting scary! See what I did there? Because of October? Spooky month? Scary? No? Worth a shot.</p>
<p>What happened in September? More letter writing! The <a href="/post/2026/08/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-snail-mail/">snail mail project</a> is going well. I keep track of the amount of outbound letters: the grand total for the last two months is <strong>20</strong> handwritten letters. If you&rsquo;d like to chime in, please let me know so we can become pen pals! More than 50% of these offline conversations fizzle out after one or two letters so it&rsquo;s only the die-hards that are willing to invest some time that get to see the best I&rsquo;ve got.</p>
<p>Previous month: <a href="/post/2026/09/august-2026/">August 2026</a>.</p>
<h2 id="games-ive-played">Games I&rsquo;ve played</h2>
<p>Contrary to the summary of August that listed two board games, I have finally picked up video gaming again after a summer holiday hiatus&mdash;which in case of a lecturer is two months. Yup. Come join us! I also started (re)playing some older <em>Castlevania</em> games <a href="/post/2026/09/october-is-spooky-video-game-month/">in anticipation of Belmont&rsquo;s Curse</a>.</p>
<p><a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/pc/the-telwynium/">The Telwynium Book 1-2-3</a> is an episodic eighties Sierra-on-line inspired high fantasy game crafted by the same person that gifted us the <em>The Drifter</em> experience. They&rsquo;re free on <code>itch.io</code> and will be bundled as one big adventure when the final episode releases somewhere in 2027. I enjoyed playing through them but there&rsquo;s nothing especially remarkable here.</p>
<p><a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/pcengine/castlevania-rondo-of-blood/">Castlevania: Rondo of Blood</a> does not need an introduction. When it comes to the release window and the platform it was released on, is the black sheep of the &lsquo;Vania family. Luckily, it got a remaster on the PSP although I&rsquo;m not a fan of those graphics. Review to follow soon.</p>
<p>The venerable Jeremy Parish recently worked through <em>Rondo</em> as part of his <em>Turbo Works Gaiden 01</em>. If you&rsquo;re interested in the weird history of this game, I recommend you watch his video instead of reading my crappy review:</p>
<figure>
	<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K9tzP1lkrDU" class="lbox"><img loading="lazy" class="img-responsive" src="https://brainbaking.com/post/2026/10/september-2026/yt-K9tzP1lkrDU.jpg" title="YouTube video K9tzP1lkrDU">
	</a>
	</figure>

<p><a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/snes/castlevania-vampires-kiss/">Castlevania: Dracula&rsquo;s Kiss</a>, also known as <em>Dracula X</em> in the US, is a &ldquo;port&rdquo; (although not really) of <em>Rondo of Blood</em> for the SNES. It&rsquo;s&hellip; not good. The &ldquo;NES Hard (TM)&rdquo; part here borders to the unfair, the level design is bland and the best parts of the original didn&rsquo;t make it to Nintendo&rsquo;s console.</p>
<p><a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/megadrive/castlevania-bloodlines/">Castlevania: Bloodlines</a> is a very good 2D action game that feels a tad different&mdash;perhaps mostly because you&rsquo;re technically playing it on SEGA&rsquo;s MegaDrive? It also released a year before <em>Vampire&rsquo;s Kiss</em> here in Europe. The soundtrack took the obvious hit but is still surprisingly catchy.</p>
<p>I started playing <em>Eastward</em> as a break from &lsquo;Vanias. The pixel art and music is amazing! And so is the first chapter but then it suddenly changes pace. The endless blabbering that even the &ldquo;skip dialogue&rdquo; button can&rsquo;t fully fast-forward is a bit painful. I&rsquo;m 8 hours in at the end of chapter 4. I still want to know where this postapocalyptic strange tale is going; but wow this game has pacing issues&hellip;</p>
